  "question_stem": "A gardener is filling an ornamental pool with water, using a hose that delivers 30 litres of water per minute. Initially the pool is empty. At time $t$ minutes after filling begins the volume of water in the pool is $V$ litres. The pool has a small leak and loses water at a rate of $0.01V$ litres per minute.\n\nThe differential equation satisfied by $V$ and $t$ is of the form $$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = a - bV.$$",
  "context_texts": [
    "$a=30$ and $b=0.01$",
    "V=3000(1-e^{-0.01t})."
  ],
